.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt RELEASE 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm release
.Nd which ABSD release this machine is serving
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints one line, the fields in the order of the release record:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
release=2026.10.02-a kernel_abi=1 fsd_protocol=2 fs_format=2 app_abi=1
.Ed
.Pp
An ABSD release is a boot image and a release tree built together under
one id.
The boot image carries the kernel, the file server, and
the SSH server;
the tree,
.Pa /releases/ Ns Ar id Ns Pa /
on the disk, carries the commands and this manual.
The file
.Pa /absd/selected
names the tree to serve.
Before it serves anything, the file server reads that tree's release
record and refuses to start unless every field states exactly what it
was built as:
.Bl -tag -width fsd_protocol
.It Cm release
the release id,
.Ql [a-z0-9.-]+ ;
.Ql dev
for a development build
.It Cm kernel_abi
the kernel's system call interface generation; every program checks the
kernel's answer when it starts
.It Cm fsd_protocol
the file server's wire protocol; every program asks the file server for
it when it starts
.It Cm fs_format
the filesystem format the file server reads
.Pq Xr filesystem 7
.It Cm app_abi
the conventions programs are started and supervised by
.El
.Pp
.Cm release ,
.Cm fsd_protocol ,
and
.Cm fs_format
are the file server's own answer;
.Cm kernel_abi
and
.Cm app_abi
are the generations
.Nm
was built for, which the kernel and the file server have already been
found to match: a program refuses to run otherwise.
.Pp
.Pa /bin
and
.Pa /share
are the selected release's
.Pa bin
and
.Pa share ;
.Pa /releases
itself is never visible.
Everything else
.Po
.Pa /etc ,
.Pa /home ,
.Pa /tmp ,
.Pa /var
.Pc
belongs to the machine and is kept when the release changes.
.Pp
.Ql uname -r
prints the id the command itself was built as.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0; 1 when no file server answers or its answer is refused; 2 when given
any argument.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
These console lines come before any session exists:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li RELEASE OK release= Ns Ar id
The file server accepted the selected release and serves it.
.It Li RELEASE REFUSED reason= Ns Ar reason
The file server refused to start: the boot ends before the SSH server
listens.
.Ar reason
is one of
.Cm no_selected_release ,
.Cm malformed_selected ,
.Cm no_release_tree ,
.Cm malformed_record ,
.Cm check_mismatch ,
.Cm release_mismatch ,
.Cm kernel_abi_mismatch ,
.Cm fsd_protocol_mismatch ,
.Cm fs_format_mismatch ,
or
.Cm app_abi_mismatch .
Boot the image of the release the disk selects, or select the release
this image belongs to.
.It Li ABI REFUSED kernel= Ns Ar n Li required= Ns Ar m
A program was started by a kernel of another system call generation
.Po
.Ar n
is
.Li -38
for a kernel older than the question
.Pc ;
it exits with status 103 before doing anything.
.It Li FSD PROTOCOL REFUSED ...
A program's file server speaks another protocol, or did not answer
within about five seconds; it exits with status 104 before doing
anything.
.El
